        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "325d926e-4fc1-5c39-8287-e871fe72a0ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cher; Brian Higgins; Stuart McLennen; Paul Barry; Steven Torch; Matthew Gray; Timothy Powell; Mark Taylor; Brian Rawling\n- Products: The Very Best of Cher; Believe; Gold; You Better Sit Down Kids\n- Companies: Warner Bros.\n- Topics: song releases; album compilations; songwriting; production\n\nFacts:\n- Cher recorded the song \"Believe.\"\n- \"Believe\" is the title track of Cher's twenty-second album, Believe, released in 1998.\n- Warner Bros. released \"Believe\" as the lead single from Cher's album Believe on October 19, 1998.\n- Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray, and Timothy Powell were credited as writers of \"Believe.\"\n- Mark Taylor and Brian Rawling produced \"Believe.\"\n- In a 2000 interview, Cher said that she also wrote part of \"Believe.\"\n- The Very Best of Cher includes Cher songs such as \"If I Could Turn Back Time,\" \"Believe,\" \"Gypsies, Tramps and Thieves,\" and \"Take Me Home.\"\n- Gold was released in 2005, two years after Cher's multi-platinum compilation album The Very Best of Cher.\n- \"You Better Sit Down Kids\" is associated with releases including a 1972 issue and Gold in 2005.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1d6b2780-7094-5d00-93a7-516adb513b31",
        "text": "Page: The Very Best of Cher. Sentence: The album includes many of Cher's most popular songs, such as \"If I Could Turn Back Time\", \"Believe\", \"Gypsies, Tramps and Thieves\" and \"Take Me Home\".\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: \"Believe\" is a song recorded by American singer-actress Cher.\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: It is the title track from her twenty-second album of the same name (1998), and was released as the lead single from the album on October 19, 1998 by Warner Bros.\nPage: Believe (Cher song). Sentence: It was written by Brian Higgins, Stuart McLennen, Paul Barry, Steven Torch, Matthew Gray and Timothy Powell, although Cher claimed later in a 2000 interview that she also wrote part, and was produced by Mark Taylor and Brian Rawling.\nPage: Gold (Cher album). Sentence: The album was released only two years after the multi-platinum \"The Very Best of Cher\".\nPage: You Better Sit Down Kids. Sentence: 1\" (1972) and \"Gold\" (2005).",
